WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.014
Tree ensembles and neural networks are two of the
most widely used model families.

00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:11.736
A soft tree is a decision tree whose splitting
rules are made differentiable,

00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:17.013
so the whole model trains by gradient descent
instead of greedy search.

00:00:17.093 --> 00:00:20.432
Ensembles of soft trees excel on tabular data,

00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:26.526
and practitioners rely on tricks like parameter
sharing, adjusting split hardness,

00:00:26.606 --> 00:00:28.458
and over-parameterization.

00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:31.728
Yet almost no theory explains why they work.

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:33.660
This paper fills that gap.
